docs {
  # Cedarrise API — Collection-Level Overview
  
  > **Version:** v1 &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Base URL:** `/api/v1` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Transport:** JSON over HTTPS (+ `multipart/form-data` for file uploads)
  
  ---
  
  ## 1. API Purpose
  
  The Cedarrise API is the backend service layer for the **Cedarrise Initiative** — a non-profit organisation running educational, mentorship, and community-outreach programmes across Nigeria. The API powers two primary surfaces:
  
  | Surface | Description |
  |---------|-------------|
  | **Admin Dashboard** | Internal web application used by staff to manage students, volunteers, outreach events, projects, receipts, metrics, and notifications. |
  | **Public Website** | Client-facing site that displays programme photo galleries, blog posts, donation flows, volunteer registration forms, and feedback collection. |
  
  ### Core Platform Modules
  
  - **ASH (After-School Hours)** — Student registration, attendance tracking, termly academic tracking, mentor assignment, feedback, exit management.
  - **TACOTS** — Scholarship recommendation, onboarding, academic tracking, feedback, exit management.
  - **Capacity Building** — Workshop/programme evaluation submissions and records.
  - **Outreaches** — Community outreach event tracking and reporting.
  - **Volunteer** — Volunteer registration, feedback, and status management.
  - **Dashboard** — Aggregate metrics (cards, charts, notifications) for programme monitoring.
  - **General** — Projects, receipts, photo gallery uploads, Google Form link management, upload page metadata.
  - **Admin** — User account and role management (RBAC).
  - **Auth** — Session-based authentication with JWT access/refresh tokens stored in HTTP-only cookies.
  - **Lookup** — Lightweight dropdown data endpoints for form select components.
  - **Clientside** — Public-facing endpoints: blog, photo carousels, donations (Paystack), homepage feedback.
  
  ---
  
  ## 2. Target Consumer
  
  This API is intended **primarily for the Cedarrise frontend application**, which includes:
  
  - **Dashboard pages** — metric cards, enrollment charts, student performance charts, institutional effectiveness charts, project management, notification centre.
  - **Admin pages** — user management, role assignment, team roster.
  - **Form pages** — ASH registration/attendance/tracking/feedback/exit, TACOTS recommendation/onboarding/tracking/feedback/exit, Capacity Building evaluations, Outreach tracker, Volunteer registration/feedback.
  - **Record management** — paginated table views with search, sort, filter, status updates, detail views, CSV downloads, and record deletion.
  - **Notification workflows** — system-generated alerts for at-risk students and inactive volunteers.
  - **File/media workflows** — photo gallery uploads, receipt image uploads, project image uploads, passport photo uploads, blog document uploads.
  - **Public website** — blog listing, programme photo carousels, donation flow, active Google Form retrieval, homepage feedback.
  
  Frontend engineers should treat this document as the canonical reference for understanding the API's surface area, conventions, and integration expectations.
  
  ---
  
  ## 3. Key Features and Functionalities
  
  ### 3.1 Authentication & Authorization
  
  | Endpoint | Method | Route | Description |
  |----------|--------|-------|-------------|
  | Login | `POST` | `/auth/login` | Authenticates with email + password; sets `cedaraccess` and `cedarrefresh` HTTP-only cookies. |
  | Logout | `POST` | `/auth/logout` | Revokes the refresh token; clears session. |
  | Session | `GET` | `/auth/session` | Validates the current session; silently refreshes expired access tokens. Returns `{ id, name, department }`. |
  
  ### 3.2 Admin — User & Role Management
  
  | Endpoint | Method | Route | Description |
  |----------|--------|-------|-------------|
  | Create user | `POST` | `/admin/users` | Creates a user account; auto-assigns the default `volunteer` role. |
  | List all users | `GET` | `/admin/users` | Returns all users (lightweight: id, name, email, department). |
  | List users (paginated) | `GET` | `/admin/listusers` | Full paginated user list with search, sort, and pagination metadata. |
  | Delete user | `DELETE` | `/admin/users/:userId` | Permanently deletes user and cascaded data. |
  | List all roles | `GET` | `/admin/roles` | Returns `volunteer`, `admin`, `superadmin` roles. |
  | List user's roles | `GET` | `/admin/roles/:userId` | Returns roles assigned to a specific user. |
  | Assign/Revoke role | `PATCH` | `/admin/roles/:userId/action` | Assigns or revokes `admin` / `superadmin` via `?action=assign&rolename=admin`. |
  
  ### 3.3 ASH (After-School Hub)
  
  **5 sub-modules**, each with Submit, List, Detail, Delete, and Download endpoints:
  
  | Sub-module | Submit | List | Detail | Delete | Download |
  |------------|--------|------|--------|--------|----------|
  | Registration | `POST` | `GET` (paginated) | `GET /:id` | `DELETE /:id` | `GET /download/ashstudent` |
  | Weekly Attendance | `POST` | `GET` (paginated) | `GET /:id` | `DELETE /:id` | `GET /download/attendance` |
  | Termly Tracking | `POST` | `GET` (paginated) | `GET /:id` | `DELETE /:id` | `GET /download/tracking` |
  | Feedback | `POST` | `GET` (paginated) | `GET /:id` | `DELETE /:id` | `GET /download/feedback` |
  | Exit | `POST` | `GET` (paginated) | `GET /:id` | `DELETE /:id` | `GET /download/exit` |
  
  **Additional endpoints:**
  - `PATCH /registration/:id/status` — Accept, reject, or reset a student (`?status=accepted|rejected|pending`).
  - `PATCH /registration/:id/assign-mentor` — Assign a mentor to an ASH student.
  
  ### 3.4 TACOTS
  
  **5 sub-modules** with the same CRUD + Download pattern as ASH:
  
  | Sub-module | Route prefix |
  |------------|-------------|
  | Recommendation | `/forms/tacots/recommendation` |
  | Onboarding | `/forms/tacots/onboarding` |
  | Tracking | `/forms/tacots/tracking` |
  | Feedback | `/forms/tacots/feedback` |
  | Exit | `/forms/tacots/exit` |
  
  **Additional endpoint:**
  - `PATCH /recommendation/:id/status` — Update admin status (`?status=NOT SELECTED|KEEP IN VIEW|SELECTED`).
  
  ### 3.5 Capacity Building
  
  | Endpoint | Method | Route |
  |----------|--------|-------|
  | Submit evaluation | `POST` | `/forms/capacity-building` |
  | List evaluations | `GET` | `/forms/capacity-building` |
  | Get detail | `GET` | `/forms/capacity-building/:id` |
  | Delete | `DELETE` | `/forms/capacity-building/:id` |
  | Download CSV | `GET` | `/forms/capacity-building/download/evaluation` |
  
  ### 3.6 Outreaches
  
  | Endpoint | Method | Route |
  |----------|--------|-------|
  | Submit outreach | `POST` | `/forms/outreaches` |
  | List outreaches | `GET` | `/forms/outreaches` |
  | Get detail | `GET` | `/forms/outreaches/:id` |
  | Delete | `DELETE` | `/forms/outreaches/:id` |
  | Download CSV | `GET` | `/forms/outreaches/download/outreach` |
  
  ### 3.7 Volunteer
  
  | Endpoint | Method | Route |
  |----------|--------|-------|
  | Register (public) | `POST` | `/volunteer/register` |
  | List volunteers | `GET` | `/volunteer` |
  | Get detail | `GET` | `/volunteer/:id` |
  | Delete record | `DELETE` | `/volunteer/:id` |
  | Update status | `PATCH` | `/volunteer/:id/status` |
  | Submit feedback | `POST` | `/volunteer/feedback` |
  | List feedback | `GET` | `/volunteer/feedback` |
  | Get feedback detail | `GET` | `/volunteer/feedback/:id` |
  | Delete feedback | `DELETE` | `/volunteer/feedback/:id` |
  | Download registrations | `GET` | `/volunteer/download/registration` |
  | Download feedback | `GET` | `/volunteer/download/feedback` |
  
  ### 3.8 Dashboard — Metrics, Charts & Notifications
  
  | Endpoint | Method | Route | Description |
  |----------|--------|-------|-------------|
  | Card numbers | `GET` | `/dashboard/cards` | Aggregate counts across all 5 programmes. |
  | Enrollment metrics | `GET` | `/dashboard/enrollment` | Chart-ready data: application trends, gender diversity, class distribution, acceptance rates, geographical distribution. |
  | Student performance | `GET` | `/dashboard/student-performance` | Graduation rates, attendance trends, test scores, dropout trends, risk distribution, TACOTS scores. |
  | Institutional effectiveness | `GET` | `/dashboard/institutional-effectiveness` | Community service hours, mentorship hours, spend per student, accumulated hours, student benchmarks. |
  | Get notifications | `GET` | `/dashboard/notifications` | Paginated system-generated alerts (filterable by `status`, `type`, `entityType`). |
  | Dismiss notification | `PATCH` | `/dashboard/notifications/:id` | Sets notification status to `dismissed`. |
  
  ### 3.9 General — Projects, Receipts, Uploads & Forms
  
  | Endpoint | Method | Route | Description |
  |----------|--------|-------|-------------|
  | Create project | `POST` | `/general/projects` | `multipart/form-data` — title, description, optional image. |
  | List projects | `GET` | `/general/projects` | All projects, ordered by status and date. |
  | Update project status | `PATCH` | `/general/projects/:id` | `?status=ongoing|completed` |
  | Delete project | `DELETE` | `/general/projects/:id` | Deletes project + Cloudinary image. |
  | Create receipt | `POST` | `/general/receipts` | `multipart/form-data` — name, amount, description, file. |
  | List receipts | `GET` | `/general/receipts` | Paginated with search and sort. |
  | Delete receipt | `DELETE` | `/general/receipts/:id` | Deletes receipt + Cloudinary image. |
  | Download receipts CSV | `GET` | `/general/download/receipts` | Full CSV export. |
  | Upload photos | `POST` | `/general/gallery` | Up to 10 images → Cloudinary (`?folder=ASH|OUTREACHES|CAPACITY_BUILDING`). |
  | Upload Google Form | `POST` | `/general/google-forms` | JSON — url, title, description, deadline. |
  | Get active Google Form | `GET` | `/general/google-forms` | Public — returns the form with a future deadline. |
  | Get upload metadata | `GET` | `/general/metadata` | Stats: photos uploaded, active projects, receipts logged, system users. |
  
  ### 3.10 Lookup — Dropdown Data
  
  | Endpoint | Route | Returns |
  |----------|-------|---------|
  | ASH students | `/lookup/ash-students` | `{ id, name, status }` for accepted ASH students. |
  | TACOTS recommended | `/lookup/tacots-recommended` | `{ id, name, status }` for `SELECTED` recommendations. |
  | TACOTS onboarded | `/lookup/tacots-onboarded` | `{ id, name }` for onboarded students. |
  | Volunteers | `/lookup/volunteers` | `{ id, name, status }` for accepted volunteers. |
  
  > All lookup endpoints are **public** (no auth) and cached with a 10-minute TTL.
  
  ### 3.11 Clientside — Public Website
  
  | Sub-module | Endpoints |
  |------------|-----------|
  | **Blog** | `POST /blogs` (create), `GET /blogs` (list, paginated), `GET /blogs/:id`, `PATCH /blogs/:id` (update), `DELETE /blogs/:id` |
  | **Carousels** | `GET /carousels/ash`, `/carousels/tacots`, `/carousels/outreach`, `/carousels/capacity-building` — programme photo galleries from Cloudinary. |
  | **Donate** | `POST /donate` (initialize Paystack), `GET /donate/callback` (verify), `POST /donate/webhook` (Paystack webhook). |
  | **Feedback** | `POST /feedback/home` — submit homepage feedback email. |
  
  ---
  
  ## 4. API Structure
  
  ### 4.1 Route Organisation
  
  All routes are mounted under the **`/api/v1`** prefix and grouped by domain:
  
  ```
  /api/v1/auth/*                    → Authentication
  /api/v1/admin/*                   → User & role management
  /api/v1/dashboard/*               → Metrics, charts, notifications
  /api/v1/general/*                 → Projects, receipts, uploads, metadata
  /api/v1/volunteer/*               → Volunteer registration & feedback
  /api/v1/lookup/*                  → Dropdown data
  /api/v1/forms/ash/*               → ASH programme forms
  /api/v1/forms/tacots/*            → TACOTS programme forms
  /api/v1/forms/outreaches          → Outreach tracker
  /api/v1/forms/capacity-building   → Capacity building evaluations
  /api/v1/blogs                     → Blog management
  /api/v1/carousels/*               → Photo galleries
  /api/v1/donate/*                  → Donation flow
  /api/v1/feedback/*                → Homepage feedback
  ```
  
  ### 4.2 HTTP Methods
  
  | Method | Usage |
  |--------|-------|
  | `GET` | List, detail, download, metrics, session verification |
  | `POST` | Create records, form submissions, login, file uploads |
  | `PATCH` | Status updates, role assignment/revocation, dismiss notification |
  | `DELETE` | Record deletion (hard delete with cascade) |
  
  ### 4.3 Request Body Formats
  
  | Format | Used By |
  |--------|---------|
  | `application/json` | Most form submissions (ASH, TACOTS, Volunteer, Outreach, Capacity Building, Blog, Donate, Feedback, Google Forms) |
  | `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` | Login, Create user, Mentor assignment |
  | `multipart/form-data` | File uploads (photos, projects, receipts, blog posts, ASH/TACOTS registrations with passport photos) |
  
  ### 4.4 Path Parameters
  
  Path parameters are consistently **UUIDs** (v4), used for:
  - `:id` — record identifier (most modules)
  - `:userId` — user identifier (admin routes)
  
  ### 4.5 Query Parameters
  
  Commonly used across listing endpoints:
  
  | Parameter | Type | Default | Description |
  |-----------|------|---------|-------------|
  | `page` | number | `1` | Page number (min: 1) |
  | `limit` | number | `25` | Items per page (min: 1, max: 100) |
  | `orderBy` | string | `desc` | Sort direction: `asc` or `desc` |
  | `sortBy` | string | `createdAt` | Column to sort by (varies per module) |
  | `status` | string | varies | Status filter (e.g. `pending`, `accepted`, `rejected`) |
  | `search` | string | — | Full-text search query (bypasses cache) |
  
  ---
  
  ## 5. Common Request/Response Patterns
  
  ### 5.1 Standard Success Response
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Descriptive success message",
    "data": { /* object or array */ }
  }
  ```
  
  ### 5.2 Paginated Response
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": [ /* records */ ],
    "meta": {
      "pagination": {
        "page": 1,
        "limit": 25,
        "totalPages": 3
      }
    }
  }
  ```
  
  Many listing endpoints also include a **`metadata`** object inside `meta` with module-specific aggregate counts:
  
  ```json
  "meta": {
    "pagination": { "page": 1, "limit": 25, "totalPages": 1 },
    "metadata": {
      "totalSubmissions": 40,
      "acceptedStudents": 10,
      "rejectedStudents": 10,
      "pendingStudents": 20
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ### 5.3 Error Response
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "error": {
      "code": "NOT_FOUND",
      "message": "Route /api/v1/unknown not found"
    }
  }
  ```
  
  | Status Code | Common Meaning |
  |-------------|----------------|
  | `400` | Validation failure (invalid fields, wrong format, missing required) |
  | `401` | Missing or invalid authentication token |
  | `403` | User lacks the required permission |
  | `404` | Resource not found / invalid credentials |
  | `409` | Duplicate resource (e.g. email already exists) |
  | `500` | Unexpected server error |
  
  ### 5.4 Full-Text Search
  
  Search is powered by **PostgreSQL GIN indexes** with weighted `tsvector` columns. When the `search` query parameter is provided:
  
  - Results are fetched **directly from the database** (cache is bypassed).
  - Sort and status filters are typically bypassed.
  - Fields are weighted (A = highest priority, D = lowest) for ranking.
  
  ### 5.5 CSV Download
  
  Download endpoints return **`text/csv`** with a `Content-Disposition: attachment` header. These are **not JSON** responses — the frontend must read them as a `Blob` and trigger a browser download.
  
  ### 5.6 Status-Based Workflows
  
  Several modules use a status lifecycle managed via `PATCH` endpoints:
  
  | Module | Status Values | Query Parameter |
  |--------|--------------|-----------------|
  | ASH Registration | `pending` → `accepted` / `rejected` | `?status=accepted` |
  | Volunteer | `pending` → `accepted` / `rejected` | `?status=accepted` |
  | TACOTS Recommendation | `KEEP IN VIEW` → `SELECTED` / `NOT SELECTED` | `?status=SELECTED` |
  | Project | `ongoing` → `completed` | `?status=completed` |
  | Notification | `active` → `dismissed` / `resolved` | N/A (PATCH body) |
  
  ### 5.7 Caching
  
  The API uses **Redis** for response caching. Key conventions:
  
  | Pattern | TTL | Example |
  |---------|-----|---------|
  | `cedarrise:dashboard:*` | 1 hour | `cedarrise:dashboard:cards` |
  | `cedarrise:{module}:{page}:{limit}:…` | varies | `cedarrise:outreaches:1:25:desc:createdAt` |
  | `cedarrise:lookup:*` | 10 min | `cedarrise:lookup:ash` |
  | `cedarrise:gallery:*` | 12 hours | `cedarrise:gallery:ash` |
  | `cedarrise:blogs:list:*` | 1 hour | `cedarrise:blogs:list:1:25` |
  
  > **Important:** Search queries **always bypass cache** and hit the database directly. Write operations (create, update, delete) **invalidate** related cache keys.
  
  ### 5.8 Chart-Ready Data (Dashboard)
  
  Dashboard metric endpoints return data in two formats, ready for direct consumption by charting libraries (e.g. Chart.js):
  
  ```typescript
  // Dataset — for bar, line, pie, doughnut charts
  {
    type: "bar" | "line" | "doughnut" | "pie",
    labels: string[],
    datasets: { label?: string, data: (number | null)[] }[]
  }
  
  // Linedata — for key-value lists
  Array<{ title: string, amount: number }>
  ```
  
  ---
  
  ## 6. Frontend Integration Notes
  
  ### 6.1 Auth Token Handling
  
  - Tokens are stored in **HTTP-only cookies** (`cedaraccess`, `cedarrefresh`) — **not** in `localStorage` or JavaScript-accessible storage.
  - The frontend does **not** need to manually attach `Authorization` headers. Cookies are sent automatically when `credentials: "include"` (fetch) or `withCredentials: true` (axios) is set.
  - The `authenticate()` middleware handles **silent token refresh** — if the access token expires, the middleware uses the refresh token to issue new cookies transparently.
  - On **`401 Unauthorized`**, redirect the user to the login page.
  
  ### 6.2 Session Verification
  
  On app load or route change, call `GET /api/v1/auth/session` to verify the user's session. The response includes `{ id, name, department }` which can be stored in frontend state.
  
  ### 6.3 Protected Routes
  
  - All **Admin**, **Dashboard**, **General**, **ASH**, **TACOTS**, **Capacity Building**, and **Outreach** endpoints require authentication.
  - Most require the `read` permission; mutations require `create`, `update`, or `delete` permissions.
  - **Public endpoints** (no auth): Login, Volunteer Registration, Lookup dropdowns, Blog listing, Carousels, Donate, Feedback, Google Form retrieval.
  
  ### 6.4 Loading States
  
  - Use loading indicators for **paginated list** requests, **detail** views, and **dashboard metrics**.
  - Dashboard metric endpoints execute multiple parallel database queries — expect slightly longer response times on the first request (before caching).
  - **CSV downloads** may be slow for large datasets — show a download progress indicator.
  
  ### 6.5 Error Handling
  
  ```typescript
  // Recommended pattern
  try {
    const res = await fetch(url, { credentials: "include" });
    const data = await res.json();
    if (!data.success) {
      // Handle application-level error
      showError(data.error?.message || data.message);
    }
  } catch (err) {
    // Handle network error
  }
  ```
  
  - **`400`** — Display validation error messages to the user (field-level where possible).
  - **`401`** — Redirect to login; session has expired.
  - **`403`** — Show "insufficient permissions" feedback; the user's role lacks the required capability.
  - **`409`** — Show duplicate resource message (e.g. "Email already exists").
  
  ### 6.6 Pagination Usage
  
  ```typescript
  // Fetch page 2 with 25 items
  GET /api/v1/forms/ash/registration?page=2&limit=25&status=pending
  
  // Use meta.pagination.totalPages for pagination controls
  // Use meta.metadata for summary stats (e.g. cards above the table)
  ```
  
  ### 6.7 Search Integration
  
  - Debounce search input (300–500ms recommended).
  - When a `search` parameter is provided, the API bypasses cache and sort/status filters — the frontend should reflect this by resetting pagination to page 1 and disabling sort/filter controls during search.
  - Clear the search parameter to return to normal cached/filtered results.
  
  ### 6.8 Form Validation Expectations
  
  The backend validates all inputs using **Zod** schemas. The frontend should perform client-side validation as a first pass, but must also handle `400 Bad Request` responses with server-side validation error messages.
  
  ### 6.9 Refreshing Dashboard Metrics
  
  Dashboard data is cached for **1 hour**. The frontend does not need to poll — simply fetch on page load. For real-time notification counts, fetch `GET /dashboard/notifications` with appropriate filters.
  
  ### 6.10 Handling Notification States
  
  - Fetch with `?status=active` to show unread/actionable notifications.
  - Filter by `type` and `entityType` for notification categorization in the UI.
  - Call `PATCH /dashboard/notifications/:id` to dismiss — update the local state optimistically.
  - The `metadata` field is a **JSON string** that must be parsed client-side; its shape varies by notification type.
  
  ### 6.11 CSV Download Pattern
  
  ```typescript
  const res = await fetch(url, { credentials: "include" });
  const blob = await res.blob();
  const downloadUrl = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
  const a = document.createElement("a");
  a.href = downloadUrl;
  a.download = "filename.csv"; // Use Content-Disposition header value
  a.click();
  URL.revokeObjectURL(downloadUrl);
  ```
  
  ---
  
  ## 7. Security and Access Control
  
  ### 7.1 Authentication
  
  - **Cookie-based JWT** — Access tokens (`cedaraccess`) and refresh tokens (`cedarrefresh`) are stored as **HTTP-only, secure cookies**, preventing XSS-based token theft.
  - The `authenticate()` middleware reads the `cedaraccess` cookie, validates the JWT, and attaches `{ id, name, department }` to the request.
  - Expired access tokens trigger an automatic refresh via the `cedarrefresh` cookie — the response includes updated cookies.
  
  ### 7.2 Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
  
  The system uses a **three-tier role model**:
  
  | Role | Permissions | Description |
  |------|------------|-------------|
  | `volunteer` | `read` | Default role assigned on user creation. Read-only access. |
  | `admin` | `read`, `create`, `update` | Can create records, update statuses, manage content. |
  | `superadmin` | `read`, `create`, `update`, `delete` | Full access including user/record deletion and role management. |
  
  The `authorize(...permissions)` middleware checks the user's role-derived permissions against required permissions for each route.
  
  ### 7.3 Permission Matrix
  
  | Permission | Used By |
  |------------|---------|
  | `read` | All listing, detail, download, and metric endpoints |
  | `create` | Form submissions, user creation, file uploads, project/receipt creation |
  | `update` | Status updates, role assignment/revocation, notification dismissal |
  | `delete` | Record deletion, user deletion |
  
  ### 7.4 CORS
  
  The API restricts origins to a whitelist:
  - `http://localhost:3002` (development)
  - `https://cedarrise.vercel.app` (production)
  
  Credentials (cookies) are allowed. Preflight responses are cached for 24 hours.
  
  ### 7.5 Webhook Security
  
  The Paystack webhook endpoint (`POST /donate/webhook`) validates the `x-paystack-signature` header using HMAC SHA-512 signature verification before processing any event.
  
  ### 7.6 Rate Limiting
  
  A rate-limiting middleware is present in the codebase (`rateLimiter.middleware.ts`) for protecting sensitive endpoints.
  
  ### 7.7 Data Sensitivity
  
  > [!WARNING]
  > The `List users for USERS Page` endpoint returns the **hashed password** field in the response. The frontend **must never** display this field to the end user.
  
  ---
  
  ## 8. Important Notes / Assumptions
  
  ### Conventions
  
  - **All routes** are prefixed with `/api/v1`.
  - **UUIDs** are used as primary keys across all tables.
  - **ISO 8601** timestamps are used for all date/time fields.
  - **Soft deletes** — Most tables include a `deletedAt` field. However, user deletion and some record deletions are **hard deletes** with cascading.
  - **Lowercase storage** — User names, emails, and many text fields are stored in lowercase/trimmed form.
  
  ### Hardcoded Values
  
  The dashboard cards endpoint has **four hardcoded values** (set to `10`) because no corresponding database tables exist:
  
  | Section | Field | Note |
  |---------|-------|------|
  | Volunteer | Partners | No partners table |
  | Volunteer | Sponsors | No sponsors table |
  | Outreaches | Partners | No outreach partners table |
  | TACOTS | Partners | No TACOTS partners table |
  
  These are annotated with `// NOT-SUPPORTED-IN-TABLES` in the service layer.
  
  ### Academic Session Scoping
  
  Dashboard metrics that reference an **academic session** derive it at runtime:
  - If the current month is **September or later** → `currentYear/nextYear` (e.g. `2026/27`)
  - If the current month is **before September** → `previousYear/currentYear` (e.g. `2025/26`)
  
  ### Public vs. Protected Endpoints
  
  | Public (No Auth) | Protected (Auth Required) |
  |------------------|--------------------------|
  | Login | All admin routes |
  | Volunteer Registration | All dashboard routes |
  | All Lookup dropdowns | All form listing/detail/delete routes |
  | Blog listing and detail | All General routes (except Google Form GET) |
  | Carousel photo galleries | All ASH/TACOTS/Capacity/Outreach management routes |
  | Donation flow | User management |
  | Homepage feedback | File uploads |
  | Google Form retrieval | CSV downloads |
  
  ### Event-Driven Side Effects
  
  The backend uses an **event emitter** pattern for side effects:
  - `donation:success` → persists donor record after verified payment.
  - Cache invalidation, email sending, and Cloudinary asset deletion are handled via events and **BullMQ job queues**.
  
  ### Notification System
  
  Notifications are generated by a **weekly BullMQ cron job** (`notification-queue`) that scans for at-risk patterns:
  
  | Type | Trigger |
  |------|---------|
  | `POTENTIAL_DROPOUT_RISK` | Student absent from latest 3 consecutive ASH sessions |
  | `LOW_ATTENDANCE_RATE` | Attendance below 75% for current term |
  | `LOW_MENTORSHIP_ENGAGEMENT` | No TACOTS tracking record for current term |
  | `SCORE_DROP_ALERT` | Post-test average dropped ≥15 points vs. prior term |
  | `VOLUNTEER_INACTIVITY` | Accepted volunteer not in any attendance record for 30 days |
  
  ### File Storage
  
  All uploaded files (photos, documents, receipts, passport photos, signatures) are stored in **Cloudinary** under organised folder paths (e.g. `/Cedarrise Initiative/ASH`, `/Cedarrise Initiative/DASHBOARD-ASSETS/PROJECTS`).
  
